<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">K'inich B'ahlam II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">7th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">K'inich B'ahlam II was a Classic Maya king of Waka', the city now called El Perú, in the north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peten">Petén</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guatemala">Guatemala</a>, in the late 7th century. He ruled as an ally of the Kaan kingdom of Calakmul and married the Kaan princess <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lady-kabel">Lady K'abel</a>, who held the title of supreme warrior. Monuments of his reign record the city's close ties to Calakmul.</p></div>
